{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/12540","id":5160666023,"node_id":"PR_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABM5mDpw","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/12540","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/12540.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/12540.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/12540","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/12540/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/12540/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/12540/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/statuses/17c4ab5539f8a38aa86b2af69a783cb595269d27","number":12540,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Stop sync runs warning `There is no current event loop` on Python 3.12 and 3.13","user":{"login":"DouweM","id":159434,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTQzNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/159434?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM","html_url":"https://github.com/DouweM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #1196\n\n### Why we make these changes\n\nOn Python 3.12 and 3.13, the first sync run in a script, whether `agent.run_sync()`, `agent.run_stream_sync()` or `Dataset.evaluate_sync()`, warns `DeprecationWarning: There is no current event loop`. Downstream projects filter it ([Vizro](https://github.com/mckinsey/vizro)). Two earlier redesigns were reverted. Decided by @DouweM on #1196: the narrow fix. Silence only that warning around the `asyncio.get_event_loop()` probe in each of the three `get_event_loop()` helpers (`pydantic_graph`, `pydantic_ai`, `pydantic_evals`), and keep loop reuse, closed-loop replacement and the undrivable-loop refusal exactly as they are. Python 3.14 raises instead, which is already handled.\n\nKnown trade-off, accepted on the issue: `warnings.catch_warnings()` changes global filter state and isn't thread-safe before 3.14, so a `DeprecationWarning` another thread emits during that call could be hidden.\n\n### New public surface\n\nNone.\n\n### User-visible behavior\n\n```\n$ python3.12 -W error::DeprecationWarning -c \"from pydantic_ai import Agent; ...; agent.run_sync('hi')\"\n# before: DeprecationWarning: There is no current event loop\n# after:  runs, no warning\n```\n\n### Verification\n\n[`test_sync_entry_point_does_not_warn_about_a_missing_event_loop`](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/12540/files#diff-33c13e0b177bacd2f02e29bcb8aea5b49e7ce34901fd8f41fefb65defba1bd33) runs each entry point under a fresh `DefaultEventLoopPolicy`, which has never had a loop set, as in a fresh interpreter, with `DeprecationWarning` turned into an error. It's skipped on 3.14+. Checked locally on 3.12: all three exit 1 on `main` and 0 on this branch.\n\n### What changes for existing users\n\nThe warning is gone on 3.12 and 3.13; nothing else changes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>PR decisions</summary>\n\n## 2026-11-04 · Narrow fix per Douwe on #1196, reviewed at d3b0e3840c5412290bea6b4680180c80b27d3b57 · iter -\n- Decision: suppress only the 3.12/3.13 DeprecationWarning around asyncio.get_event_loop() in the graph, ai and evals helpers; subprocess test per entry point\n- Why: Douwe's decision on #1196 (2026-11-04); pydanty triaged twice without opening a PR; review 1 findings (evals skip, narrow -W filter) remediated, review 2 current\n- Source: https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/1196\n</details>\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] No **breaking changes** in accordance with the [version policy](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/blob/main/docs/version-policy.md).\n- [x] Any permitted **compatibility impact** has a label, warning, migration and release note, and an exact API-check waiver if the gate reports it.\n- [x] **PR title** is fit for the [release changelog](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/releases).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nStops the first sync run per script from warning `There is no current event loop` on Python 3.12 and 3.13. `agent.run_sync()`, `agent.run_stream_sync()`, and `Dataset.evaluate_sync()` now suppress that `DeprecationWarning` around the `asyncio.get_event_loop()` probe in the three `get_event_loop()` helpers; loop reuse, closed-loop replacement, and Python 3.14's raise behavior are unchanged.\n\n- Trade-off: `warnings.catch_warnings()` changes global filter state and isn't thread-safe before 3.14, so another thread's `DeprecationWarning` during that call could be suppressed.\n- Adds in-process tests that recreate a fresh loop policy (no current loop) and run each sync entry point with the warning treated as an error; the evals case is skipped when `pydantic-evals` isn't installed.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 17c4ab5539f8a38aa86b2af69a783cb595269d27. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/12540?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"View guided diff\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n","labels":[{"id":7110547176,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABp9JW6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"Report that something isn't working, or PR implementing a fix","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9947550442,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAACUOuS6g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/size:%20S","name":"size: S","description":"Small PR (≤100 weighted lines)","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12513945186,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAAC6eOmYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/pkg:core","name":"pkg:core","description":"pydantic-ai-slim, pydantic-ai and examples (pydantic_ai_slim/, examples/)","color":"5319e7","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T19:54:41Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T23:49:01Z","closed_at":"2026-11-04T23:48:59Z","merged_at":"2026-11-04T23:48:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"8f3d45734cbe18b3e5e5434947086ef285ead5df","assignee":{"login":"DouweM","id":159434,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTQzNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/159434?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM","html_url":"https://github.com/DouweM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DouweM/subscrip